# 2. Product objective

At launch, when an investor opens a resale property, the screen should immediately communicate:

1. a real property from the canonical 24-property portfolio;
2. a current share price and ownership state;
3. approximately one year of **historical price context**;
4. useful high/low/change/period context;
5. a polished secondary-market experience;
6. an unmistakable **PBD! — mean: Platform bootstrap data** disclosure;
7. real recent trades only when they actually exist;
8. a clear live-market empty state before the first real trade;
9. safe buy/sell/order-book behavior.

The desired perception is "this product has history" — **not** "we fabricated customers and transactions."

The highest-value work is therefore:

> **Secondary property detail → historical chart → PBD disclosure → truthful live transition → market/order-book UX → optional platform bootstrap metrics.**

